The Missouri native announced the cancellations on Friday (Oct. 23), citing laryngitis and vocal cord tears.

&#8220;Hey guys. i am heartbroken to share after multiple doctor visits i have laryngitis and vocal cord tears and have been ordered to go on medication and full vocal rest for at least two weeks,&#8221; she wrote on her Instagram Story. &#8220;Because of this, i am forced to cancel the remaining UK/EU dates to avoid permanent damage to my voice. full refunds will be available at point of sale.&#8221;

Slayyyter continued: &#8220;My team and i are already working on rebooking shows for next year and i hope to have news to share very soon to make it up to you. I know how much time and effort is spent to come out to a show. some of you have traveled, some of you have made costumes, and i am completely devastated to not be able to give you the shows you were planning for.&#8221;

The pop star is promising to make it up to the European fans with shows at a later date. &#8220;We are working hard to figure out a time to return so i can deliver an even bigger and better show for you all,&#8221; she added. &#8220;I hope you know i will make this up to you. lots of love to you all. thank you for making this tour so special.&#8221;

As reported by People , Slayyyter previously revealed that she &#8220;completely&#8221; lost her voice and doctors ordered her to cancel shows in Copenhagen (Oct. 22) and Hamburg, Germany (Oct. 23).

The tour was slated to resume on Saturday (Oct. 24) in Warsaw, Poland, and run through Nov. 5. Slayyyter&#8217;s last performance came on Oct. 18 in Paris.

The &#8220;Beat Up Chanel$&#8221; singer has no remaining performances after wiping the rest of her 2026 slate clean, and will return to the stage in February with a handful of Australia and New Zealand shows before heading to South America in March. Slayyyter will also headline her first arena show in the Big Apple on June 21 at Madison Square Garden.

While she won&#8217;t be performing, Slayyyter has new music on the way. The pop provocateur&#8217;s Wor$t Man in America is slated to arrive on Dec. 4, and serves as a nine-track &#8220;brother&#8221; album to Wor$t Girl in America , which arrived in March and reached No. 22 on the Billboard 200.
